> Out of curiosity, how do you detect that a player has finished the
> mines or sokoban?

I decided to call them "completed" when you pick up the Sokoban prize, or
the guaranteed luckstone in the mines.  Obviously, that has some drawbacks,
but I had a hard time coming up with anything better.

Of course, that means that many ascenders will not be listed as doing
either.  Since the achievements were geared towards tracking the progress of
players who don't ascend regularly, I don't think that's all that serious.

The other ways that I considered detecting it would have been to watch for
when you filled all the trapdoors in the final Sokoban level, and when you
reached the bottom level of the Mines.  However, it seemed a bit strange to
me to have the game record completion when most players will not consider
themselves to have accomplished the real goal.

